/// Mints and verifies authenticated session tokens.
///
/// Tokens have the shape `v1.<user-hex>.<expiry>.<session-id>.<mac>`, where
/// the MAC covers every preceding field. Two properties follow, and an
/// application needs both:
///
/// * **Unguessable.** `session_id` is 16 CSPRNG bytes, so neighbouring tokens
///   cannot be enumerated from one observed token — the defect a
///   clock-plus-counter token has.
/// * **Unforgeable.** The MAC binds the user, the expiry and the generation,
///   so an end user cannot edit any of them, and a token cannot be extended
///   by rewriting its expiry.
///
/// The `generation` field is what makes logout-everywhere expressible
/// without a session enumeration: the application keeps a per-user counter,
/// mints tokens carrying its current value, and bumps it to strand every
/// token issued before the bump. [`SessionService::verify_fenced`] applies
